The boundary integral is noise-dominated at the coverage you train at

Pure numerics — exact solid-angle kernel on a sphere, no learning involved — so it bounds what any model of this class can do at this sampling rate. Kernel validated against 4π to ten digits.

At a trace query (the DrivAerML surface task), the double layer splits into:

