What this would explain (hypothesis — flagged as such)

Four results the program treats as independent collapse into one mechanism, if this carries to the learned model:

- Exact kernels contribute 0–8%. Exactness of a kernel is worthless when the estimator around it has 385% error. The factorial compared exact vs learned members in a regime where neither can compute the integral — it measured a noise floor.
- Trace dominates at 3.8%×. The own-panel term is the one piece computed exactly and always retained. It's also the largest.
- The two trace sub-mechanisms are near-perfect substitutes. Both deliver the same single reliable number. Once either does, the other is redundant — exactly the measured ~96% / ~96% / +6%.
- The 2.34× ID gap to GeoTransolver. It never attempts the cancellation; smooth learned pooling is a low-variance aggregate. It's solving a better-conditioned estimation problem, not approximating better.

If that holds, your central bet wasn't refuted — it was never tested at a sampling rate where it could pay off.

The fix is algebraic, and free

For a closed surface the total solid angle from the exterior side is exactly zero. So

$$u(x)=\sigma(x)\underbrace{\textstyle\sum_j\Omega_j}_{=,0}+\sum_j\Omega_j(\sigma_j-\sigma(x))=\sum_j\Omega_j(\sigma_j-\sigma(x))$$

The rewritten integrand is small everywhere — near the query Ω is huge but the difference →0; far away the difference is O(1) but Ω is tiny. The cancellation is removed analytically instead of numerically. Classical BEM singularity subtraction; what's new is using it as a variance-reduction device for a subsampled operator.

Identical kernel, identical samples, identical coverage — only the arrangement differs:

┌──────────┬───────────┬────────────────┬───────────────┐
│ coverage │ plain SNR │ subtracted SNR │ std reduction │
├──────────┼───────────┼────────────────┼───────────────┤
│ 0.11%    │      0.65 │           4.16 │          6.4× │
├──────────┼───────────┼────────────────┼───────────────┤
│ 35%      │     13.06 │          93.49 │          7.5× │
└──────────┴───────────┴────────────────┴───────────────┘

6.4× on std is ~41× variance — the accuracy of 4.5% coverage obtained at 0.11%, and it crosses the estimator from noise-dominated to signal-dominated. Zero parameters. It needs exactly one input: σ(x), the query's own coefficient — which trace mode already computes as the own-cell readout. The mechanism your factorial found load-bearing is precisely the ingredient the fix requires.

