Pre-registered, before implementing anything

P1 exact-only beats MLP-only by more than the current ~7%; P2 trace's 3.8× shrinks; P3 absolute ID improves 10–30% (modest, because the model spent training compensating for noise it will no longer see). Each with its falsifier. Confounds stated: the identity needs a closed boundary, and the single-layer member has a different non-zero total requiring its own constant — derivable, not free.

This bears directly on your framing: global interaction is one of the four properties a PDE solver must have, and the measurement says the sampling protocol was destroying it while leaving the local term intact.
